  "solution": "**Logic :** (2nd number × 2) = (3rd number + 1st number)\n\n**Given :**\n\n \n• (9, 20, 31)\n\n20 × 2 = 31 + 9\n\n40 = 40 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• (38, 49, 60)\n\n49 × 2 = 60 + 38\n\n98 = 98 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (63, 60, 65)\n\n60 × 2 = 65 + 63\n\n120 ≠ 128 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (15, 20, 31)\n\n20 × 2 = 31 + 15\n\n40 ≠ 46 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (25, 69, 45)\n\n69 × 2 = 45 + 25\n\n138 ≠ 70 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (14, 24, 34)\n\n24 × 2 = 34 + 14\n\n48 = 48 (LHS = RHS) \n\nHence, \"Option - (4)\" is the correct answer.",
